WEBVTT

00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:09.768
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Miriam really liked her job – it was very interesting.

00:00:10.832 --> 00:00:18.466
I worked from home, so I was with the children a lot and I loved it. In general life was good.

00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:22.520
It was quite cheap – cheaper than in the UK.

00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:31.158
We joined a sports club, where the children learned to swim, and I played a lot of tennis, one of my favourite sports.

00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:35.459
The people in Durham were very friendly.

00:00:36.156 --> 00:00:38.489
They often invited us to their homes.

00:00:39.191 --> 00:00:45.035
It was easy to meet people at the sports club, or at the university where Miriam worked.

00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:48.875
And there were so many new places to see!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.135
At weekends we visited some of the beautiful national parks.

00:00:54.604 --> 00:00:57.468
They were very different from English parks!

00:00:58.275 --> 00:01:05.429
In one park there was a sign saying <i>Don’t disturb the snakes</i> – Sacha loved it!

00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:11.747
I also remember a trip to a country music festival at a blueberry farm.

00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:13.721
It was fantastic.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:21.217
First we listened to the music, and then we picked a lot of blueberries – they’re Elena’s favourite fruit.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:26.201
But after that trip she didn't want to eat a blueberry for at least two weeks!

00:01:27.138 --> 00:01:33.609
We stayed in Durham for a year. After that we returned to England, because my wife’s job finished.

00:01:34.239 --> 00:01:40.621
But we loved our life in the USA, and we're thinking of going back there in maybe two or three years.